# Fortuna Labs — build log & launch checklist

Everything in /projects/fortunalabs was built autonomously. This file is the handover.

## What exists

```
fortunalabs/
├── site/index.html                  # fortunalabs.net landing page (static, deploy-ready)
├── products/
│   ├── pine/FortunaCoil.pine        # TradingView indicator v1
│   ├── pine/FortunaCoilStrategy.pine# TradingView strategy/backtester version
│   ├── mt5/FortunaCoil.mq5          # MetaTrader 5 EA with source
│   └── docs/                        # setup guide + methodology note
```

All ports are parameter-for-parameter faithful to the validated research strategy
(Fortuna_V3 strategies/idea-s6qtcghc46, "coil-volume-breakout"): range 40, vol avg 20,
surge 2.0x, coil percentile 0.40 over 252 bars, ATR 14 x 3.0 trail, 10-bar time stop.

## Verification status (honest)

- Pine scripts: written carefully against Pine v5 semantics but NOT compiled — no Pine
  runtime here. Paste into TradingView's Pine Editor and fix any compile complaints
  before shipping (likely minor; ta.percentrank / var handling are the spots to check).
- MQL5: same — not compiled. Compile in MetaEditor before selling.
- No TradingView screenshots yet (need a TradingView login to run bar replay).

## Launch checklist for Tim

1. **Legal (do first):** one session with an Australian lawyer re: ACL + whether the
   indicator/EA sales and any future Telegram alert service need an AFS licence.
   The copy is already framed conservatively (general information, historical results
   labelled), but get it checked.
2. **Compile & screenshot:** verify both Pine scripts in TradingView; capture 2-3 chart
   screenshots showing COIL signals; drop into site/index.html.
3. **Payments:** create a Gumroad account (fastest) or Stripe Payment Links; wire the
   Buy buttons to them ($199 indicator, $349 EA bundle option).
4. **Deploy:** `site/index.html` is a single static file — Netlify/Vercel/GitHub Pages,
   point fortunalabs.net at it. Email hello@fortunalabs.net (Zoho Forward or similar).
5. **Later products:** research newsletter ("The Graveyard") next-cheapest to ship;
   Telegram signals service needs legal sign-off + running the fleet rail live.

## Claim discipline (binding)

Every performance number on the site traces to F003 / forward-results.json in
Fortuna_V3: OOS Sharpe ~1.27, PF 2.50, 21 trades, Binance top-10 alts daily, costs
~24bp RT, lookahead passed, forward window flat. Honest forward expectation per our own
shrinkage analysis: 0.4-0.7 Sharpe. Never quote anything higher in public material.
